#### Problem 6
I have a bag of $N$ white marbles. I paint $20$ of the marbles black. Later, my sister pulls out $30$ marbles, and I tell her that my best guess (i.e., the mean answer) is that $10$ of them will be black. How many marbles are in the bag?

_Answer_:
$\frac{20}{N} = \frac{10}{30}$ gives $N = 60$.

