### Section 2
#### Problem 1
A spherical balloon is inflated at a constant rate of $4$ cubic inches per second. When the volume of the balloon is at $\frac{9\pi}{2}$ cubic inches, at what rate is the surface area of the balloon expanding?

_Answer_: 
$\frac{dv}{dt} = 4$ and $\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 = \frac{9\pi}{2} \Rightarrow r = \frac{3}{2}$. Also, $\frac{ds}{dt} = 4\pi \cdot 2r \cdot \frac{dr}{dt} = \frac{2}{r} \frac{dv}{dt} = 2 \times \frac{2}{3} \times 4 = \frac{16}{3}$

